24| *   `{code,message,hint}` the strict probe throws: a missing binary
25| *   (ENOENT on spawn or on a thrown error) reads as `MUSE_MSP_BIN_MISSING`
26| *   with the install fix; a killed/timed-out child reads as
27| *   `MUSE_MSP_TIMEOUT`; anything else reads as
28| *   `MUSE_MSP_DISCOVERY_FAILED` with the run-it-by-hand hint. Pure
29| *   classifier — no spawning, safe to unit-test with fake results.
30| * @example describeMuseSpawnFailure({ spawnError: Object.assign(new Error('spawn muse ENOENT'), { code: 'ENOENT' }), bin: 'muse' }).code => 'MUSE_MSP_BIN_MISSING'
